1. Incident response: remote-access compromise
A user opened a malicious script from a fake legal email, which installed a hidden remote-access tool Nov
12. The account was disabled, attacker infrastructure was blocked, and the device is going to reimage; a 14
day hunt found no other affected devices. A second remote-access attempt on Nov 16 was blocked
automatically.
I investigated the device across Defender and the anti-ransomware console. I confirmed the agent was
active and in Prevention but raised no alert, checked the isolation status (the first request expired while the
laptop was offline and was resubmitted), and reviewed Intune security settings and ASR rules.
I recommend: allowing only approved remote-support tools via Intune application control; moving the
"unusual executable" ASR rule from Audit to Block; confirming web blocking is enforced outside Edge; a
vendor root-cause case; and targeted user awareness.
