5. Purview assessment and implementation planning
I reviewed the Purview baseline and configuration across audit, DSPM, DLP, sensitivity labels, Copilot
protection and governance, and I built implementation and audit planning covering classification, labels, DLP,
Endpoint DLP, retention, evidence and ownership.
I found the credit card DLP rule first showed user notifications without blocking; a later screen showed
external-only blocking selected. Saving and enforcement still need confirmation, and admin alerts and
incident reports were off.
I aligned the plan to IT-first, with HR, Legal, Finance and Transportation added gradually once IT is stable,
and a low-admin approach: audit mode first, automated alert triage, short data-driven asks.
I asked the partner to add the Microsoft 365 Copilot location to DLP, so Copilot doesn't surface highly
confidential content.
Next: confirm saved configurations, define pilot acceptance criteria, test with synthetic data.
