6. 24/7 automation: AI triage and close
Weekend help-desk shifts ended Nov 12. I created the AI Triage and Close architecture to deliver after-hours
coverage for High and Medium incidents without adding headcount AI investigates and recommends,
workflow rules validate and record decisions, and humans approve high-impact actions. I recommended the
promptbook path through the Logic App connector as the baseline, subject to testing.
I also designed a Sentinel-first Weekend Responder that protects first and reviews the next business day:
low-impact containment runs automatically, high-impact actions go through a short approval, and a Monday
summary shows everything that happened.
Next: validate invocation, authentication, escalation, failure handling and closure safeguards before
production.
7. Agent implementation, identity and permissions
I led a working session with the implementation partner on implementing the new Security Copilot agents. I
validated our setup 2 compute units, owner roles, plugins), compared agent identities in Entra, and
narrowed the failure to a missing agent identity and blueprint on the Security Analyst Agent; we
redeployed it together. I reviewed agent roles in Unified RBAC (the Phishing Triage Agent has its own) and
proposed the Threat Intelligence Briefing and Security Analyst agents as candidates before custom builds.
Next: set up the new auto-triggered alert triage agent (needs a Global Admin), verify least-privilege roles,
and keep troubleshooting custom-agent publishing HTTP 500.
8. Sentinel and Defender incident correlation
I reviewed the tenant correlation setting (disabled) and its effect on Sentinel rules and automation. I
recommend piloting correlation on selected rules before a wider change, keeping exceptions where separate
incidents are needed; any automated closure must reassess every alert on the incident.
9. ISO evidence and governance
I connected pilot monitoring and agent-access reviews to ISO evidence (configuration records, approvals,
health-check results, ownership) and prepared questions on permission justification, access reviews,
logging and revocation. The ISO assessment lands the week of Nov 23, remediation runs in December, and
transition completes Feb 1. I offered to own the monthly Sentinel and automation governance input.
